// BUG-862: `naked` is accepted but the IR path does NOT emit
// __attribute__((naked)) — the function still gets a compiler prologue and
// epilogue, so it is not truly naked (docs/limitations.md).
//
// Re-enabling the attribute is a real migration (every existing asm test omits
// an explicit `ret` and would SIGILL), so it stays deferred. What is NOT
// acceptable is the SILENCE: a reset handler or context-switch primitive written
// against the documented meaning of `naked` gets a hidden prologue and fails on
// the target with nothing said at compile time — and on bare metal that does not
// fault, it just misbehaves.
//
// This test is wired through tests/test_zer.sh `warn_check`, which asserts the
// warning is actually printed. Delete it in the same commit that re-enables the
// attribute.
naked void boot_entry() {
    asm("nop");
}

u32 main() {
    return 0;
}
